message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Grounded Document Extraction: provenance-grounded field extraction with a bounded verification loop"
abstract: >-
  An extracted field must carry provenance back to the specific source tokens it
  was read from, and a field whose provenance does not verify is abstained on
  rather than emitted. Extraction becomes selection plus verification rather than
  generation, which makes "this value appears nowhere in the document" a
  structural impossibility rather than a statistic.
